# The kiwi firmware: a KiwiSDR or a Web-888 as the knob's own receiver
# (VFO_RADIO=kiwi), over KiwiSDR's protocol -- listened to and tuned, and
# another of them a swipe away. It only receives.
#
# WiFi only, without the USB networking of sdkconfig.usbnet: the receivers
# are on the internet, and the USB link has no route there -- the knob is the
# DHCP server on it, on a link with no gateway. Leaving TinyUSB out also frees
# the internal RAM its buffers take, and keeps the serial console on the cable.

# The receiver's socket, a /status read or the page's Test beside it, the
# web page's and the log's.
CONFIG_LWIP_MAX_SOCKETS=16
# ...and every address a receiver's name stands for, tried in turn. Safe only
# without SNTP: lwIP's cache then writes them all where SNTP keeps one.
CONFIG_LWIP_DNS_MAX_HOST_IP=4

# AES in software, as every firmware now: the engine's DMA takes its bounce
# buffers from internal RAM. The receivers' TLS -- both ears at once on
# https:// ones, a Test beside them -- and the update downloads run without
# it.
CONFIG_MBEDTLS_HARDWARE_AES=n
